Subject: [PATCH] rfp: per-site noise on rendered audio, and one screen size for every computer

Two things a page reads to recognise a computer, which the engine's
fingerprinting protection does not cover without full resistFingerprinting:

1. What an OfflineAudioContext renders. The samples depend on the engine
   build and the processor, and FingerprintJS and PrivacyTests.org read them
   back (an oscillator through a compressor, then a sum of the samples). A new
   target, AudioRandomization, moves each rendered sample by at most one part
   in ten thousand, by an amount that comes from the per-site, per-session key
   the canvas noise already uses and from the samples themselves. Two sites
   read different values; one site reads the same values again for the same
   sound. Every sample gets its own step, so the noise cannot be divided out
   as one factor. Only the buffer an offline rendering returns is covered.
   What a page reads from a context that plays is not changed, and neither
   is, by this patch, what a node inside the offline graph itself hands to
   script while it renders (an AnalyserNode, a ScriptProcessorNode, an
   AudioWorklet): patch 0016 gives those the same noise. The per-site
   key is made for this target alone too, without the canvas noise.

2. The screen's size. A new target, ScreenSizeConstant, makes screen.width and
   height, the available area (at 0,0) and the device-width and device-height
   media queries say 1920 by 1080 for every document the protection applies
   to. It is decided per document by the engine's own check, so a site the
   person exempts, the browser's own pages and extensions read the real size,
   and a frame or a pop-up is asked for itself. Responsive design mode and
   WebDriver BiDi's screen emulation come first, as they do today, and a
   page being printed keeps the paper's size. The
   existing ScreenRect target (the window's inner size as the screen) only
   helps with fixed window sizes, which Nulavio does not use.

Neither target is in the engine's default set: Nulavio turns them on in
privacy.fingerprintingProtection.overrides (ADR 0016, ADR 0019, issue #79).

Owner: Nulavio maintainers
Upstream: not proposed. Mozilla's own audio protection is tracked in its
bug 1358149; a constant screen is a different trade-off from ScreenRect.
